  "representation": {
    "intrinsic": "Default Array allocation derives prototypes from the existing current-realm intrinsic table; it never reads mutable global Array or invents another constructor authority.",
    "length": "Array.from uses shared LengthOfArrayLike. Only ArrayCreate owns the ordinary Array length bound; custom species observe the converted length. Callback validation precedes map species construction.",
    "final_set": "Array.from array-like and Array.prototype.slice use the existing array-like length Set after indexed definitions. TypedArray.from retains its different contract.",
    "reduction": "Removed global/prototype reads, duplicated length conversion and premature map/slice length checks. Existing operations own coercion, property effects and abrupt completion."
  },
